    "q-67813": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67813",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A skydiver falls $40$ feet in $\\frac{5}{6}$ seconds. What is the unit rate of feet fallen per second?",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the unit rate of feet per second, we divide the number of feet, $40,$ by the number of seconds, $\\frac{5}{6}$, as follows: \n\n$$\n40÷\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40÷\\frac{5}{6} & =40\\times \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{1}\\times \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\times 6}{1\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{240}{5} \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $48$ feet per second.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
