    "q-67905": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67905",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A leaking paddling pool loses $6$ liters of water in  $\\frac{2}{3}$ hours. How much water will it lose in $1$ hour?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out how much water the pool will lose in $1$ hour, we can compute the unit rate of liters of water lost per hour. We do this by dividing  the number of liters, $6,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{2}{3}$, as follows:     \n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6÷\\frac{2}{3} & =6\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\times 3}{1\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the pool will lose $9$ liters of water in $1$ hour.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-67905-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$8$ liters",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"34\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> liters"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-67905-b",
