    "q-169441": {
      "dom_id": "step-q169441",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Owen takes $\\frac{4}{5}$ hours to do $24$ math exercises. How many exercises can he do in $1$ hour?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the number of exercises Owen can do in $1$ hour, we compute the unit rate of exercises per hour. We do this by dividing the number of exercises Owen does, $24,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{4}{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n24÷\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24÷\\frac{4}{5} & =24\\times \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\times 5}{1\\times 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{4} \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Owen can do $30$ exercises in $1$ hour.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
