    "q-67843": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67843",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A plane can travel $\\frac{3}{5}$ of a mile in $6$ seconds.  What is the unit rate of miles traveled per second?",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the unit rate of miles per second, we divide the number of miles, $\\frac{3}{5},$ by the number of seconds, $6$, as follows:    \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}÷6\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}÷6 & =\\frac{3}{5}÷\\frac{6}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 2\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\times 1}{5\\times 2\\times \\cancel{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{1}{10}$ miles per second.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
