    "q-67840": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67840",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Johnny walked $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a mile in  $7$ minutes, keeping an even pace. How many miles did he walk in $1$ minute?",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the number of miles Johnny  walked in $1$ minute, we can compute the unit rate of miles per minute. We do this by dividing the number of miles, $\\frac{3}{8},$ by the number of minute, as follows:   \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷7\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}÷7 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{8\\times 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{56}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, Johnny walked  $\\frac{3}{56}$ miles in $1$ minute.",
