    "q-67874": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67874",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "A race car covers $\\frac{4}{5}$ of a lap in  $2$ minutes.  What is the unit rate of laps covered per minute?",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the unit rate of laps per minute, we divide the number of laps, $\\frac{4}{5},$ by the number of seconds, $2$, as follows:     \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}÷2\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}÷2 & =\\frac{4}{5}÷\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\times 1}{5\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times 2}{2\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\times 2}{\\cancel{2}\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{2}{5}$ laps per minute.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
