    "q-67967": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67967",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Riding his electric bike, Matt can go $\\frac{1}{2}$ of a mile in $\\frac{3}{4}$  minutes. What is the unit rate of miles covered per minute?",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the unit rate of miles per minute, we divide the number of miles, $\\frac{1}{2},$ by the number of minutes, $\\frac{3}{4}$, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}÷\\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\times 4}{2\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times 2}{2\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\times 2}{\\cancel{2}\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate is $\\frac{2}{3}$ miles per minute.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
