    "q-67829": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67829",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Jim ran $\\frac{5}{6}$ of a mile in $\\frac{1}{5}$ of an hour. How many miles can Jim run in $1$ hour?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the number of miles Jim can run in $1$ hour, we can compute the unit rate of miles per hour. We do this by dividing the number of miles, $\\frac{5}{6},$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{1}{5},$ as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}÷\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{6}÷\\frac{1}{5} & =\\frac{5}{6}\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\times 5}{6\\times 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{6}=4\\,\\text{R}1=4\\,\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Jim can run $4\\,\\frac{1}{6}$ miles in $1$ hour.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
